                <pb facs="1008" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg914"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received July 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 919.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Rev. Mr. Baird, a missionary educator, has gone to Bitlis to supply the place of
                    the Rev. George Knapp. In pursuance of the agreement with me by the Turkish
                    Government that when a missionary was withdrawn another should take his place,
                    every facility was afforded to Mr. Baird by traveling teskereh, etc., by the
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
